## AI Idea

### AI-Assisted Healthcare Support Request Analysis

The application uses AI to help NGO support staff review incoming requests faster.

When a user submits the support form, the request description is sent from the React frontend to the Express backend.

The backend sends the relevant request information to the AI service.

The AI generates:

1. A short summary of the request
2. A support priority – Low, Medium, or High
3. A suggested action for the NGO support team

### Example

A user submits:

> "My grandmother is unable to travel to the pharmacy and needs help getting her regular medicines."

The AI may generate:

```text
Summary:
The user is requesting assistance with accessing regular medicines
for an elderly family member.

Priority:
Medium

Suggested Action:
Contact the requester and check whether a volunteer can assist
with medicine collection or delivery.
```

The AI is only used for organizing and summarizing requests. It is not used for medical diagnosis or treatment recommendations.

---

## NGO Use-Case

The application can be used by a healthcare NGO or community organization to collect support requests from people who need assistance.

For example, users may request:

* Medical assistance
* Medicine delivery support
* Transport assistance
* Elderly care
* General healthcare-related support

Instead of receiving unstructured messages, the NGO team can receive a summarized request with a suggested handling priority.

This can help volunteers:

* Understand requests quickly
* Identify requests that may need faster follow-up
* Organize incoming support requests
* Reduce manual work when reviewing requests
* Connect people with suitable community support

---

## How It Works

```text
User
  |
  v
React + Tailwind Form
  |
  v
Express REST API
  |
  +----------------+
  |                |
  v                v
MongoDB          OpenAI
  |                |
  |                v
  |          AI Summary
  |          Priority
  |          Suggested Action
  |                |
  +-------+--------+
          |
          v
     React UI
          |
          v
   Request Summary
```

