## Installation

Clone the project:

```bash
git clone YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
```

Go to the frontend:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
```

Go to the backend:

```bash
cd ../backend
npm install
```

---

## Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file inside the backend folder.

```env
PORT=5000

MONGODB_URI=

GEMINI_API_KEY=
```

For the frontend, create:

```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
```


---

## Running the Project

### Start Backend

```bash
cd backend
npm run dev
```

Backend will run on:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

### Start Frontend

Open another terminal:

```bash
cd frontend
npm run dev
```

Frontend will run on:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

---

## API

### Submit Support Request

```text
POST /api/support/analyze
```

Example request:

```json
{
  "name": "Rahul Kumar",
  "email": "rahul@example.com",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "supportType": "Medicine Support",
  "message": "I need help getting medicines for my grandmother."
}
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "name": "Rahul Kumar",
    "supportType": "Medicine Support",
    "summary": "The user needs assistance accessing medicines for an elderly family member.",
    "priority": "Medium",
    "suggestedAction": "Contact the requester and check whether a volunteer can assist."
  }
}
```

---

## Database

MongoDB is used to store support requests.

A support request can contain:

```text
name
email
phone
supportType
message
aiSummary
priority
suggestedAction
createdAt
```

MongoDB Atlas can be used as the cloud database during deployment.

---

## Deployment

### Frontend

The React frontend can be deployed using Vercel.

Build command:

```bash
npm run build
```

### Backend

The Express backend can be deployed using Render.

Start command:

```bash
npm start
```

### Database

MongoDB Atlas can be used for the production database.

